{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787123390,"nonce":"xHaNWvs/Yr9xiDIumRapSemR43k=","message":"⛔ **THE BODY ABOVE IS WRONG AND I WROTE IT. Corrected here rather than deleted, so the mistake stays visible. The title has been replaced.**\n\nI filed this from a peer's accurate flag and then diagnosed it one level short of the builder. Verified since, by reading the code rather than the SPEC:\n\n- `ViewService.actions` (`internal/notification/service/view.go:598-626`) emits exactly four entries across three ids: `oto.unack`, `oto.ack`, `oto.noop.runbook`, `oto.noop.silence`.\n- A repo-wide grep for `oto.snooze` / `oto.unsnooze` returns **nothing**.\n- `internal/channels/service/interactions.go:35-43` is a closed set: `oto.ack`, `oto.unack`, `oto.noop.`. `ActionUnacknowledge`'s own comment says it outright — *\"It is the ONLY withdrawal this surface has, because ack is the only thing it writes.\"*\n\n**So, clause by clause:**\n- *\"A snoozed card still offers `Snooze`\"* — **no card offers it.** There is no button to swap.\n- *\"the action row contradicts the field above it\"* — there is no contradiction, there is an **absence**. The `*Notifications*` field `77886a8` added is the only place a snooze appears on a card.\n- *\"clicking `Snooze` on an already-snoozed alert … the operator learns which by doing it in a channel other people are reading\"* — that was the most vivid line in the ticket and it describes an experience **no operator can have**, because the button does not exist.\n\n**The scope call was wrong too.** \"Small — the action builder reading a field that exists\" is true only of the final swap. The actual work is a snooze affordance carrying §B.8.3's five presets (30 m · 1 h · 4 h · 24 h · 7 d), which in Slack means an overflow or a modal — and `overflowMenu` is already at its documented five-option ceiling, where its own comment warns a sixth is `invalid_blocks` and takes the card with it. Plus two new ids in a deliberately closed vocabulary whose file says \"Add ids; never rewrite one\", plus handler branches onto `grouping`'s `SnoozeAs`/`UnsnoozeAs` ports (`internal/grouping/service/ports.go:165`), which DO exist. **Medium at least, and it contains a design decision nobody has made.**\n\n**What survives from the original filing:** §B.8.6 and §P-17 really are half-implemented and nothing recorded it until this was filed. And `77886a8` did put `SnoozedUntil` on the view, so once a Snooze button exists the Unsnooze swap genuinely is trivial — it is the last ten percent, not the ticket.\n\n⚠️ How this happened, because it is the third false-premise incident on this branch and the first that was mine: §B.8.6 says the `Snooze` action \"**becomes**\" `:bell: Unsnooze`, which presupposes machinery that was never built. I read the spec clause and stopped before the builder. The ticket even says \"The demonstration. Not run — read\" — and that is precisely where the reading stopped. The other two were `f299d8a` (wrong about its own ADR) and `7570090` (wrong that a generation is packed into a UUID). **Read the cited source, not the clause that cites it.**","files":null}]}